This file lists the third-party models, runtimes and components that Parlora
Tutor depends on, adapts or recommends. Each one keeps its own licence or
terms, which apply to that component and are not changed by Parlora Tutor's
licence. Components marked "planned" arrive with the voice pipeline (Phase 1)
and are not yet installed by this repository.

Model weights are never stored in this repository; they are downloaded by the
user from their original source and are subject to that source's terms.


Speech recognition
------------------

Whisper (OpenAI) — model weights and reference code — MIT License. Planned.
  https://github.com/openai/whisper

faster-whisper (SYSTRAN) and CTranslate2 (OpenNMT) — MIT License. Planned.
  https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper


Speech synthesis
----------------

Kokoro-82M (hexgrad) — model weights — Apache License 2.0. Planned.
  https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M

misaki (hexgrad) — grapheme-to-phoneme library — MIT License. Planned.
  Used without extras. Parlora Tutor also adapts misaki's table that maps
  espeak-ng IPA phonemes to Kokoro phonemes; that code is used under the MIT
  License with attribution.
  https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki

kokoro-onnx (thewh1teagle) — MIT License. Planned.
  Parlora Tutor does not install this package (it pulls in GPL code); it
  adapts parts of its ONNX runner under the MIT License, with attribution.
  https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx

espeak-ng — GNU General Public License v3.0 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later).
  Planned. Used only as a separate executable for words missing from the
  pronunciation dictionary (out-of-vocabulary words): Parlora Tutor starts the
  `espeak-ng` program as a separate process, passes it one word and reads back
  the phonemes. No espeak-ng code is linked, imported or contained in this
  repository. The server image installs the Debian `espeak-ng` package when the
  user builds it locally; Parlora Tutor does not publish container images. Any
  distributed image that contains espeak-ng must meet the GPL-3.0 terms for that
  component. See docs/adr/0004-kokoro-g2p-and-gpl-boundary.md.
  https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng

spaCy and the en_core_web_sm model (Explosion) — MIT License. Planned.
  https://github.com/explosion/spaCy


